# Project: document vault SaaS

You are working on a production SaaS app, not a prototype or demo. A solo,
non-professional-engineer founder is directing this build through chat
prompts and will not manually review most of your code line by line — treat
correctness, security, and clarity as non-negotiable, not nice-to-haves.

**Stack**: TypeScript everywhere, strict mode, no `any` without a comment
justifying it. Next.js 14+ (App Router) for the web app. A separate
long-running Node.js worker service for background jobs — never put
background/queue logic in Vercel serverless functions. PostgreSQL via
Supabase (Auth + Database + Row Level Security). Cloudflare R2 for file
storage. OpenAI API for document classification. Stripe for billing. Redis
(Upstash) + BullMQ for the job queue.

**Monorepo layout** (Turborepo): `/apps/web`, `/apps/worker`,
`/packages/shared-types`, `/packages/api-client`, `/supabase/migrations`,
`/cloudflare-worker` (the inbound-email Worker, deployed separately via
Wrangler). Do not create top-level folders outside this structure without
asking first.

**Non-negotiables**: Row Level Security on every user-data table before it's
usable. No secret ever appears in client-side code or gets committed to git.
All plan-limit and billing decisions are resolved server-side, never trusted
from the client. Every background job is idempotent and safe to retry.

Security rules live in `010-security.mdc`, coding conventions in
`020-conventions.mdc`, and agent behavior rules in `030-agent-behavior.mdc`.
All three are equally binding on every task, regardless of what a specific
prompt asks for.
